# Plain `pub const NAME: uN = ...` that deliberately differs from the kernel
# symbol of the same name.
#
# The plain-const pass (#266) checks every constant whose name the kernel also
# defines verbatim. That is almost always what you want — but a handful of
# names are legitimately nlink-local and collide with an unrelated kernel
# symbol, or hold a mask/sentinel rather than the kernel's value.
#
# Each entry needs a written reason. "It's fine" is exactly what a drifted
# constant would also say — the same discipline as
# audit-uapi-constants.allowlist, for the same reason.
#
# Format: one bare constant name per line, `#` comments.

# (empty — every name-matching constant currently agrees with the kernel)
